Content:
By Adriano Marchese

Endeavour Silver's second quarter silver production was higher than a year earlier, but missed the company's targets, it said.

The miner reported consolidated silver production of 1.94 million ounces, a 31% rise in output from the prior-year period. The higher production is attributed to the additional ounces from Kolpa. Production in the prior-year period included two months of production from the Kolpa mine in Peru after it was acquired in early May 2025.

Silver production at its Mexican mine Guanacevi was 30% lower, largely due to 35% lower silver grades but partially offset by slightly higher throughput.

Gold production rose 35% to 10,474 ounces, thanks to the contribution from Terronera. Guanacevi saw a 21% decline in gold production.

Write to Adriano Marchese at adriano.marchese@wsj.com
