Content:
Samsung Electronics (SSNLF) is preparing to unveil a shorter, wider Galaxy Z Fold 8 on July 22 as it tries to stay ahead of Apple's  rumored push into foldable phones.

The company will host its Galaxy Unpacked event in London, where reports say it will introduce 3 foldable phones alongside wearables such as a smartwatch and clip-on wireless earbuds. The headline device is expected to be a new Fold 8 variant with a passport-style footprint.

Bloomberg reported that Samsung will still debut successors to the Galaxy Z Fold 7 and Galaxy Z Flip 7, but the wider Fold 8 model could offer a more immersive video experience and better multitasking. Samsung has also teased the new design across social media.

the launch matters because Samsung is trying to defend its foldable-phone lead before Apple enters the category. The next catalyst is the July 22 event, where pricing and availability will show how aggressively Samsung plans to compete.
