Content:
By Julia Amann

Daily traffic through the Strait of Hormuz has held steady despite fresh attacks on commercial ships that triggered a flare-up in tensions in the Mideast.

According to ship-tracking company Kpler, 36 vessels crossed the waterway on Monday and 41 on Tuesday, the day after the attacks. That's on par with last week's average of about 40 crossings a day.

This item is part of a Wall Street Journal live coverage event. The full stream can be found by searching P/WSJL (WSJ Live Coverage).
