Content:
Hungary's central bank cut its base rate by 25 bps to 6.00% last month in a decision that was backed by 10 policymakers, while one rate setter proposed a 50 bps cut, the minutes of its June 23 policy meeting showed on Wednesday.

"In the Council’s June assessment, there would be an opportunity to implement a series of steps consisting of three 25-basis-point interest rate cuts during the summer months, after which the September Inflation Report would provide guidance regarding the interest rate path," the minutes showed.

"The Council noted that the inflation outlook had improved significantly."
