Content:
By Dean Seal

Shares of Palladyne AI gained after the company's preliminary second-quarter results showed big jumps in its revenue and backlog.

The stock was up 5.6% at $5.67 in premarket trading. Shares had already grown 26% year-to-date as of Tuesday's close.

The defense and industrial technology company said revenue in the fiscal quarter ended last month is seen rising to $5.8 million from just $1 million a year earlier. Analysts polled by FactSet are expecting $4.6 million.

The company's backlog, meanwhile, has skyrocketed to $24 million from $1.7 million in the year-earlier quarter.

Write to Dean Seal at dean.seal@wsj.com
