Content:
Consumer prices in Chile stood flat in June from the previous month, data from statistics agency INE showed on Wednesday, not meeting market expectations of a decline.

Inflation slowed down from a 0.2% increase registered the prior month, but compared with expectations of a 0.21% decline from a Reuters poll of economists.

Prices rose in eight of the 13 sectors surveyed on a monthly basis, INE said, with insurance and financial services registering the highest rise.

"Food and non-alcoholic beverages saw price increases in ten of their 15 categories. The most significant increase was in bread, cereals, flour, and pasta," INE added.

Annual inflation in the world's largest copper producer hit 4.3%, INE added, accelerating from the 3.9% registered in the previous month.

With the latest rise, inflation went over the central bank's target range of 2% to 4%.
