Content:
The Baltic Exchange's dry bulk freight index, which tracks rates for ships carrying dry bulk commodities, fell on Wednesday, pressured by weakness in the capesize vessel category.

• The main Baltic index , which tracks rates for capesize, panamax and supramax vessels, fell 4 points, or 0.1%, to 2,871.
• The capesize index (.BACI) was down 34 points, or 0.8%, at 4,480.
• Average daily earnings for capesize vessels (.BATCA), which typically transport 150,000-ton cargoes including iron ore and coal, fell $310 to $37,130.
• However, Iron ore futures rose on Wednesday, supported by improving Chinese warehousing demand and a climb in property sales.
• The panamax index (.BPNI) gained 15 points, or 0.7%, to 2,245.
• Average daily earnings for panamax vessels (.BPWT), which usually carry 60,000 to 70,000 tons of coal or grain, increased $140 to $20,209.
• Among smaller vessels, the supramax index (.BSIS) was up 10 points, or 0.6%, at 1,686.
