Publicis Groupe is likely to report similar second-quarter organic revenue growth to the first, and back its full-year guidance when it reports half-year earnings on July 16, Citi analyst Ciaran Donnelly writes. The French advertising group's Sapient business will be a headwind to growth as it suffers a full quarter hit from the war in the Middle East, Citi says. "We expect FY26 guidance to be reiterated, though it seems increasingly unlikely that Sapient will deliver growth this year," Donnelly writes. Shares are down 3.3% at 85.22 euros. (ian.walker@wsj.com)
