Content:
By Connor Hart

Energy stocks rose after President Trump said he believed his ceasefire deal with Iran was over and oil prices jumped.

Shares of Exxon Mobil were up 1.6%, to $143.93, in premarket trading Wednesday. Meanwhile, Chevron's and Conoco Phillips' stock each climbed 1.7%, to $177 and $110.30, respectively.

Shares of BP gained 1%, to $38.99. Occidental Petroleum's stock increased 2.6%, to $53, while shares of Diamondback Energy edged 2.3% higher, to $184.67.

Trump's comments came after another round of Iranian attacks on ships in the Strait of Hormuz. The remarks are a sign that diplomacy with Iran has stalled under the preliminary peace agreement he signed in mid-June, The Wall Street Journal reported.

Trump also tore into Iran's leadership. "They're liars, they're cheats, they're sick people," he told reporters at a NATO summit in Ankara on Wednesday.

"Now I'll let our wonderful negotiators keep talking if they want, but I don't see it."

Oil prices climbed after Trump's comments, with Brent crude futures about 5% higher at $73.93 a barrel.

Write to Connor Hart at connor.hart@wsj.com
